    "comment": {
      "comments": [
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12432985/comment/12742821",
          "id": "12742821",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=shaie",
            "name": "shaie",
            "key": "shaie",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Shai Erera",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Asia/Jerusalem"
          },
          "body": "Remove assert v != null and added a test case.\n\nFunny, but it's as if CTL itself could cause this bug. If you call ctl.get() w/o setting anything first, it creates a WeakReference and set the initValue(), which is ... null !. The first call to get() will return null, the second would fail. :)\n\nBTW, TestCloseableThreadLocal is under o.a.l.index. Shouldn't it be under o.a.l.util? Can whoever assigns this to himself move it?",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=shaie",
            "name": "shaie",
            "key": "shaie",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Shai Erera",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Asia/Jerusalem"
          },
          "created": "2009-08-13T13:25:15.417+0000",
          "updated": "2009-08-13T13:25:15.417+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12432985/comment/12742830",
          "id": "12742830",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mikemccand",
            "name": "mikemccand",
            "key": "mikemccand",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael McCandless",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "bq.  If you call ctl.get() w/o setting anything first, it creates a WeakReference and set the initValue(), which is ... null\n\nI don't think that's right?\n\nIt calls initialValue(), and only if that returns a non-null value will it set it.  Else it doesn't call set?  (So calling get() twice in a row not having called set shouldn't hit an exception).  I think?",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mikemccand",
            "name": "mikemccand",
            "key": "mikemccand",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael McCandless",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "created": "2009-08-13T14:12:52.264+0000",
          "updated": "2009-08-13T14:12:52.264+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12432985/comment/12742831",
          "id": "12742831",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=shaie",
